# W5-DOCS-2: TRACKING IS THE DEFAULT for documentation.
#
# This used to be a hand-maintained allowlist, one line per file. That is precisely how 101
# strategy documents ended up outside git for months while the code was safe in a remote:
# deny-by-default made tracking something a human had to remember, and nobody did. The
# safety property that justified it is now automatic instead of manual - `check:docs-secrets`
# fails the build on any credential-shaped value in a tracked doc, and runs on push.
#
# `*.md` only, so binaries and exports (docs/.DS_Store, dumps, images) stay ignored by
# default and have to be added deliberately.
!docs/*.md

kpopquiz_*.md
quizz_*.md
login_redesign.html
mascot_placement_prototype.html
supabase/migrations/_misplaced/
pinterest-pins/
scripts/fonts/
# Intermediate avatar-layer staging (21MB of keyed/recolored source PNGs).
# Shipped runtime assets live in apps/quiz/public/avatar/; regenerate sources
# with scripts/recolor_hair.py.
avatar-assets/

# nested git worktrees (fork workers)
.worktrees/

# Graphify build artefact (GRAPHIFY TRIAL, 2026-08-17). 19MB, and derived from a codebase
# that changes every commit, so a tracked copy is stale on the next merge. We inverted
# docs/ to track-by-default only because check:docs-secrets made its safety property
# automatic; a tracked graph has the mirror problem with NO equivalent gate, and a stale
# graph nobody notices is exactly the failure mode this trial was run to test for.
# Rebuild with: graphify . --update
graphify-out/
